#' Random Number Generation from the Curve Distribution
#'
#' Generates random observations from the Curve distribution
#' using the inverse transform sampling method.
#'
#' Random values are generated by first obtaining independent
#' uniform random variables U on the interval [0, 1] and then
#' applying the quantile function:
#'
#' \deqn{
#' X = Q(U) = 1 + \sqrt[3]{8U}.
#' }
#'
#' @param n Number of observations to generate.
#'   Must be a non-negative integer.
#'
#' @return A numeric vector containing n random observations
#'   from the Curve distribution.
#'
#' @details
#' This function uses the inverse transform method to generate
#' random numbers. The resulting observations belong to the
#' interval [1, 3].
#'
#' The random number generation process can be made
#' reproducible using [set.seed()].
#'
#' @examples
#' rcurve(10)
#' @export

rcurve <- function(n) {
  u <- stats::runif(n)
  qcurve(u)
}
